From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 31 Oct 2026 11:02:24 -0643
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: exynos: google: zumapro-tegu: Add the MAX77779
 charger

The MAX77779's charger answers at 0x69 on the same bus as its fuel gauge
and USB-C port controller. Describe it, and name it as the fuel gauge's
power supply, so the max77779-charger driver binds from the device tree
and the battery reports charging through it.

This node has no interrupt yet; the chip charges on its own, and the
driver reports its state and offers charge inhibit.

power-supplies is also a device link: the fuel gauge now waits for the
charger to probe, so if the charger driver is missing or fails to probe,
the battery stays deferred with it.

Signed-off-by: W4HO <87742609+W4HO-ham@users.noreply.github.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts | 10 ++++++++--
 1 file changed, 8 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
index 848dd690c..e373d05a7 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/exynos/google/zumapro-tegu.dts
@@ -345,8 +345,8 @@ led {
 };
 
 /*
- * The MAX77779's bus: its fuel gauge and its USB-C port controller, a sink
- * with no link to the USB controller's role yet.
+ * The MAX77779's bus: its USB-C port controller, a sink with no link to the
+ * USB controller's role yet, its fuel gauge and its charger.
  */
 &hsi2c6 {
 	clock-frequency = <950000>;
@@ -377,6 +377,12 @@ fuel_gauge: fuel-gauge@36 {
 		compatible = "maxim,max77779-fg";
 		reg = <0x36>;
 		shunt-resistor-micro-ohms = <2000>;
+		power-supplies = <&charger>;
+	};
+
+	charger: charger@69 {
+		compatible = "maxim,max77779-charger";
+		reg = <0x69>;
 	};
 };
 
